From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: viewports, name scopes, owned TemplateBindings, library x:Uid, PathIcon, ThemeShadow, BindingOperations, routed events

Windows Terminal's settings page (WinUI 2's NavigationView) showed an empty menu. Its ItemsRepeaters realize their items from EffectiveViewportChanged, which elements were never told; they look for an IScrollAnchorProvider above them (the ScrollViewer). The template setup failed earlier on several missing pieces: FindName did not reach a ContentControl's content its template does not show; a compiled {TemplateBinding AutomationProperties.Name} renamed the part (it took FrameworkElement.Name); an application class composed over a Panel lost the application's own members (ItemsRepeaterScrollHost.ScrollViewer); ThemeShadow, UIElement.Shadow, PathIcon, FontIcon statics 2 and 3, BindingOperations.SetBinding and UIElement's routed event identifiers with AddHandler were missing. The items' texts come from x:Uid strings, which in a library's markup (ms-appx:///Library/...) are the library's (Library/Resources), not the application's. All of these are added; ThemeShadow is kept, not drawn; routed handlers for events this implementation does not raise yet (pointer, gesture, manipulation, drag) are accepted.
